  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Market Driven Irrigated Horticulture Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lesotho Health and Horticulture Compact - Market Driven Irrigation Horticulture (MDIH) Project; The objective of the Market Driven Irrigated Horticulture Project (the &quot;MDIH Project&quot;) to increase rural incomes related to commercial horticulture, including for women, youth, and the rural poor, and establish a sustainable and inclusive model of irrigation, water resource, and land management. The Project plans to achieve this objective by making a catalytic investment in irrigation in partnership with commercial investors, providing local capacity building and technical assistance, and supporting reforms in land, water, and gender with the expectation that these interventions will spur sustainable and inclusive private sector growth and investment in the horticulture sector.</narrative>
  </description>
